  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Les Bains Canins, on rue Georges Clemenceau in Cannes, goes beyond classic grooming: the salon also offers a wellness area with spa and massage for dogs and cats.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the salon's official website (lesbainscanins.com), it is closed on Monday and Sunday. It opens Tuesday to Friday from 9:30am to 1pm and 2pm to 6:30pm, and on Saturday from 9:30am to 1pm. All sizes are accepted: the site distinguishes small and medium dogs from large dogs, up to 120 kg.</p>
      <h3>Services and prices published by the salon</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>"Les Minis": 30 minutes, from 28 to 58 EUR.</li>
        <li>Small and medium dogs ("Fripouille"): about 2.5 hours, from 55 to 85 EUR, including a Dead Sea mud relaxation massage, wash, cut or stripping, drying, nails and ears.</li>
        <li>Large dogs ("Vitamines"): about 4 hours, from 75 to 150 EUR, up to 120 kg.</li>
        <li>Cats and rabbits: 3 hours, from 85 to 125 EUR.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The salon also announces a "bike taxi" to collect your pet at home in Cannes and Le Cannet, and day care during holidays, without conditions or prices on the site. The spa is described as an independent treatment room with four types of care: aromatic baths with Dead Sea salts, massage with essential-oil gels, thalassotherapy with clay and Dead Sea mud wrap, and paw pad treatment. Spa-only prices are not detailed: ask by phone before booking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Worth checking: prices are given as ranges and duration depends on the breed; call 04 93 39 54 81 for a quote and to book.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cannes town centre and rue d'Antibes, with its shops, are within walking distance from rue Georges Clemenceau.</p>
    </div>

